g('exporting-to-the-usa-isf-10-2', 'abroad', 'Shipping to the USA|ISF 10+2 and customs entry',
  'What exporters must know to ship to the US: ISF 10+2 filing, importer of record, customs bond, entry and the penalty for filing late.',
  'US Customs and Border Protection asks for data about ocean cargo before it is loaded. The US importer, not the Indian exporter, files most of it.',
  [('ISF 10+2', 'The Importer Security Filing needs 10 data elements from the importer and 2 from the carrier. It must be filed at least 24 hours before the cargo is loaded at the foreign port. Late or wrong filing can lead to a penalty of thousands of dollars per violation.'),
   ('Who does what', ['Importer of record (US): files the ISF, holds a customs bond and files the entry.', 'Exporter: provides the data on time, such as manufacturer, country of origin, HTS code and the stuffing location.', 'Carrier: files the manifest and the vessel stow plan.']),
   ('Duty', 'US duty is by HTS code, with extra tariffs for some origins and products. Rates change often, so check the latest before you quote a price.'),
   ('Other agencies', 'Food and drugs need FDA prior notice and registration. Plants and wood need USDA rules. Some goods need other agency permits.')],
  [('Is the ISF needed for air cargo?', 'No. It is for ocean cargo.'),
   ('Can the Indian exporter file the ISF?', 'Only if it acts through a licensed US broker as the importer, which is unusual.'),
   ('What if I ship DDP?', 'Then the seller organises the US clearance, usually through a US broker and the broker bond.')],
  ('landed-cost-calculator', 'Open the landed cost calculator'))
g('exporting-food-to-the-usa-fda-prior-notice', 'abroad', 'Exporting food to the USA|FDA registration and prior notice',
  'How to export food to the US: FDA facility registration, prior notice, the US agent, labelling and what the importer must do.',
  'Food shipped to the United States is regulated by the FDA. The exporter and the importer each have duties.',
  [('Exporter duties', ['Register the food facility with the FDA and name a US agent.', 'Comply with the food safety rules and the labelling rules of the US.', 'Give the importer the data for the prior notice.']),
   ('Prior notice', 'A notice of the incoming food must reach the FDA before arrival. The minimum time depends on the mode: shorter by road and longer by sea. The importer or the broker files it.'),
   ('Importer duties', 'A US importer must have a foreign supplier verification programme to check the safety of the supplier.'),
   ('At the border', 'The FDA can sample, hold or refuse the food. Refused food must be exported or destroyed under supervision.')],
  [('Do I need to register for a spice?', 'Yes. Most food facilities need registration.'),
   ('Who is the US agent?', 'A person in the US who can speak for the facility. Some service companies offer it.'),
   ('Are there special rules for seafood?', 'Yes. Seafood has its own safety rules and often needs more documents.')],
  ('document-checker', 'Open the document checker'))
g('exporting-to-the-european-union', 'abroad', 'Exporting to the European Union|EORI, CE, REACH and import VAT',
  'What an Indian exporter needs to ship to the EU: the importer EORI, customs value, CE marking, REACH, labels and VAT on import.',
  'The EU works as one customs territory, with one tariff and common product rules. The importer does most of the customs work.',
  [('Customs', ['The EU importer needs an EORI number to file the declaration.', 'Duty depends on the TARIC code and the origin. Check whether a preference applies.', 'Pre-arrival safety data is filed by the carrier, and sometimes by the importer, under the ICS2 system.']),
   ('Product rules', ['CE marking and a declaration of conformity for many industrial and consumer goods.', 'REACH for chemicals, and rules on food contact and cosmetics.', 'Labelling in the languages of the country of sale.']),
   ('VAT', 'Import VAT is charged at the border at the rate of the member state. A registered importer can reclaim it.'),
   ('Plant and food', 'Plants, food and animal products need health or phytosanitary certificates, and some are inspected at border posts.')],
  [('Does India get low duty in the EU?', 'For most goods India no longer gets the generalised preference, so check the current rate for your code.'),
   ('Who handles the CE marking?', 'The manufacturer, and the EU importer must check it.'),
   ('Do I need an EU agent?', 'For some products an authorised representative is needed.')],
  ('hsn-code-finder', 'Open the HSN code finder'))
g('exporting-to-the-united-kingdom', 'abroad', 'Exporting to the UK|EORI, UKCA and import VAT',
  'What an exporter needs to ship to the UK: importer EORI, UK tariff, product marks, import VAT and the status of the India UK trade deal.',
  'The UK has its own customs system and tariff, separate from the EU since Brexit.',
  [('Customs', ['The UK importer needs a GB EORI number.', 'Duty follows the UK Global Tariff and the origin of the goods.', 'Declarations are made on the UK customs declaration service.']),
   ('Product rules', 'The UKCA mark and, for some products, the CE mark are accepted. Food, plants and animal products have their own checks, including health certificates.'),
   ('VAT', 'Import VAT is charged at the border, and registered importers can use postponed accounting to avoid paying it up front.'),
   ('Trade agreement', 'India and the UK have agreed a trade deal. Check whether it is in force and what rate it gives for your product before you quote.')],
  [('Is there a de minimis?', 'Low value consignments have special VAT and duty rules. Check the current limits.'),
   ('Who is responsible for UKCA?', 'The manufacturer or the UK importer, as the product rules say.'),
   ('Can I use a UK agent?', 'Yes, many exporters do.')],
  ('hsn-code-finder', 'Open the HSN code finder'))
g('exporting-to-the-uae', 'abroad', 'Exporting to the UAE|duty, documents and the India CEPA',
  'How to export from India to the UAE: customs duty, importer code, documents, the India UAE CEPA rate and clearance at Dubai and Abu Dhabi.',
  'The UAE is one of India biggest markets. Customs is quick and duty is low, and the trade agreement can lower it further.',
  [('Duty', 'Most goods pay the GCC common external tariff of 5 percent. Some goods are exempt and some, such as tobacco and alcohol, pay more. VAT of 5 percent applies on import.'),
   ('CEPA', 'The India UAE Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement can give a lower or zero duty on many goods, if you meet the origin rule and hold the certificate of origin.'),
   ('Documents', ['Commercial invoice, packing list and bill of lading or airway bill.', 'Certificate of origin, if you claim the CEPA rate.', 'Product certificates for food, cosmetics and others, as the authorities ask.']),
   ('Clearance', 'The importer needs a customs code with the emirate customs office. Free zones have their own rules and re-export is simple.')],
  [('Is the UAE duty 5 percent for everything?', 'No. Check the tariff for your code.'),
   ('Do I have to attest documents?', 'It depends on the goods and the buyer. Ask the importer.'),
   ('Can I ship to a free zone?', 'Yes. Duty is paid when the goods leave the zone for the local market.')],
  ('trade-agreement-preference-checker', 'Open the trade agreement checker'))
g('exporting-to-saudi-arabia-saber', 'abroad', 'Exporting to Saudi Arabia|SABER, SFDA and customs',
  'How to export to Saudi Arabia: SABER product conformity, shipment certificates, SFDA for food and drugs, and customs clearance.',
  'Saudi Arabia requires product conformity checks on many regulated goods before they ship. Cargo without the certificates can be refused.',
  [('SABER', 'The SABER platform is where importers register products and get the certificate of conformity for regulated goods. A shipment certificate of conformity may also be needed for each shipment, issued by an approved body.'),
   ('SFDA', 'Food, drugs, cosmetics and medical devices come under the Saudi Food and Drug Authority and have their own approvals.'),
   ('Customs', 'The importer clears through the customs system. Duty follows the GCC tariff, usually 5 percent, plus VAT.'),
   ('Plan ahead', 'Ask the buyer which products and certificates apply before you ship. Rules change often.')],
  [('Who gets the certificate?', 'The importer registers on SABER and the exporter or the manufacturer supplies the test and product data.'),
   ('Is the invoice attested?', 'Check with the buyer and the bank.'),
   ('Is Arabic labelling needed?', 'For many consumer products, yes.')],
  ('document-checker', 'Open the document checker'))
g('exporting-to-nigeria-form-m-and-paar', 'abroad', 'Exporting to Nigeria|Form M, PAAR and port clearance',
  'How exports to Nigeria are cleared: the importer Form M, the pre-arrival assessment report, duty and the common causes of delay.',
  'Nigeria asks the importer to file before the goods ship. A shipment without the right approvals can be stuck at Lagos for weeks.',
  [('Form M', 'The importer registers the order on the Form M through a Nigerian bank before the goods are shipped. The exporter invoice should match the Form M details.'),
   ('PAAR', 'A pre-arrival assessment report is created by customs and is needed to clear the goods. The importer or the agent applies for it with the invoice and the Form M.'),
   ('At the port', 'Duty, levies and the inspection follow. Product conformity and permits apply for some goods, such as food, drugs and used items.'),
   ('Tips', ['Do not ship before the Form M is approved.', 'Keep the invoice, description and values identical in all documents.', 'Use an experienced agent in Lagos. Rules and fees change often.'])],
  [('Is a pre-shipment inspection needed?', 'The rules have changed over time. Ask the importer for the current rule.'),
   ('How long does clearance take?', 'It varies, from a week to much longer if documents do not match.'),
   ('Who pays the duty?', 'The importer, unless the sale is DDP.')],
  ('document-checker', 'Open the document checker'))
g('exporting-to-brazil-from-india', 'abroad', 'Exporting to Brazil|licence, NCM and taxes',
  'What an Indian exporter should know to sell in Brazil: importer registration, import licence, the NCM code, the stack of taxes and the clearance.',
  'Brazil is a large market with a complex tax system. The importer handles clearance, but the exporter needs to give the right data.',
  [('The importer', 'A Brazilian importer needs registration with customs (RADAR) and, for most goods, an import licence in the Siscomex system before shipping.'),
   ('The code', 'Brazil uses the Mercosur NCM, with eight digits, based on the HS. Our Brazil NCM finder helps map your product.'),
   ('Taxes', 'Several taxes stack on one another: import duty, IPI, PIS and COFINS, and the state ICMS. The landed cost is often much higher than the duty alone.'),
   ('Paperwork', 'Commercial invoice, packing list, BL, and certificates for regulated goods from the health, agriculture and standards bodies. Documents may need to be in Portuguese for some agencies.')],
  [('Do I need a local agent?', 'Most exporters sell to a Brazilian importer who handles the clearance.'),
   ('Is there a trade deal with India?', 'India and Mercosur have a limited preferential agreement, for a list of products.'),
   ('How long does clearance take?', 'Allow extra time for licences and inspections.')],
  ('brazil-ncm-finder', 'Open the Brazil NCM finder'))
g('exporting-to-australia-biosecurity', 'abroad', 'Exporting to Australia|biosecurity and container rules',
  'How to export to Australia: biosecurity rules, clean containers, wood packaging, fumigation, permits and customs.',
  'Australia is strict on pests and diseases. The paperwork and the container condition matter as much as the duty.',
  [('Biosecurity', 'The department of agriculture inspects cargo, packing and containers. Wood packaging must meet ISPM 15. Plants, food, animal products and used goods need permits or certificates.'),
   ('Clean containers', 'Containers must be clean of soil, seeds and pests, inside and out. A dirty container can be sent for cleaning at your cost.'),
   ('Customs', 'The importer needs an import declaration and pays GST. Duty is low on most goods and there is a trade deal with India for some goods.'),
   ('Tips', ['Ask the importer for the import conditions of your product before you ship.', 'Use treated pallets and keep the paperwork.', 'Inspect the container before loading.'])],
  [('Do used goods need cleaning?', 'Yes. Used machinery and vehicles must be clean of soil and plant material.'),
   ('What is BICON?', 'The online system that lists the import conditions for goods.'),
   ('Who handles the inspection?', 'The biosecurity officers, at the port or at an approved place.')],
  ('document-checker', 'Open the document checker'))
g('shipping-cargo-to-nepal-via-india', 'abroad', 'Shipping cargo to Nepal via India|ports, rail and transit',
  'How cargo reaches Nepal through India: Kolkata and Visakhapatnam ports, rail to the border, transit documents and clearance in Nepal.',
  'Nepal is landlocked and most of its sea trade moves through Indian ports. Cargo travels in transit under the India Nepal treaty.',
  [('The routes', 'Containers arrive at Indian ports such as Kolkata and Haldia and Visakhapatnam, then go by rail or road to the border or to an inland depot in Nepal.'),
   ('Documents', 'Bill of lading, invoice, packing list and the transit declaration. Cargo moves under customs control, with seals, from the Indian port to the Nepal customs point.'),
   ('Clearance', 'Nepal customs clears the cargo and charges duty at the destination. Indian customs sees the cargo as in transit, so Indian duty does not apply.'),
   ('Plan for', 'Rail schedules, border delays and the free days of the shipping line, because detention can build up on the long trip.')],
  [('Is Bhutan the same?', 'Similar, with its own routes and rules.'),
   ('Do I need a bond?', 'The transit rules need a guarantee or a bond.'),
   ('Can a forwarder handle it all?', 'Yes. We can arrange the move from the port to the border.')],
  ('india-transit-times', 'See India transit times'))
